IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pip-nouns`

-- Schedule 1, Part 3: the mobility activities table.
--
-- Same shape as the daily living table (pip-sch1-daily-living-table.l4): one row for each
-- descriptor, copied from the table lines of the text by a script that is not kept in this folder.
--
-- The register of legislation.gov.uk lists one effect in force on 2017-03-16 that its
-- editors had not applied to this text (words substituted in the table of Part 3 by
-- the amending regulations of 2017, reg 2(4)); see NOTES.md. The table is encoded as
-- it is printed in the deposited text.

§ `Schedule 1, Part 3: the mobility activities table`

§§ `Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1: Planning and following journeys`

-- Row of the table: activity, letter, points, words
-- src:624 | | 1. Planning and following journeys. | a. Can plan and follow the route of a journey unaided. | 0 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor a (src:624)
`row for mobility 1a` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter a`, 0, "Can plan and follow the route of a journey unaided."

-- src:625 | | b. Needs prompting to be able to undertake any journey to avoid overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant. | 4 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor b (src:625)
`row for mobility 1b` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter b`, 4, "Needs prompting to be able to undertake any journey to avoid overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant."

-- src:626 | | c. Cannot plan the route of a journey. | 8 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor c (src:626)
`row for mobility 1c` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter c`, 8, "Cannot plan the route of a journey."

-- src:627 | | d. Cannot follow the route of an unfamiliar journey without another person, assistance dog or orientation aid. | 10 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor d (src:627)
`row for mobility 1d` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter d`, 10, "Cannot follow the route of an unfamiliar journey without another person, assistance dog or orientation aid."

-- src:628 | | e. Cannot undertake any journey because it would cause overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant. | 10 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor e (src:628)
`row for mobility 1e` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter e`, 10, "Cannot undertake any journey because it would cause overwhelming psychological distress to the claimant."

-- src:629 | | f. Cannot follow the route of a familiar journey without another person, an assistance dog or an orientation aid. | 12 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 1, descriptor f (src:629)
`row for mobility 1f` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`, `letter f`, 12, "Cannot follow the route of a familiar journey without another person, an assistance dog or an orientation aid."

GIVEN d IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 1`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`the row of a descriptor of mobility activity 1` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `mobility 1a` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1a`
    WHEN `mobility 1b` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1b`
    WHEN `mobility 1c` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1c`
    WHEN `mobility 1d` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1d`
    WHEN `mobility 1e` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1e`
    WHEN `mobility 1f` THEN JUST `row for mobility 1f`
    WHEN `no descriptor of mobility activity 1 applies` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2: Moving around`

-- Row of the table: activity, letter, points, words
-- src:630 | | 2. Moving around. | a. Can stand and then move more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided. | 0 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor a (src:630)
`row for mobility 2a` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter a`, 0, "Can stand and then move more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided."

-- src:631 | | b. Can stand and then move more than 50 metres but no more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided | 4 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor b (src:631)
`row for mobility 2b` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter b`, 4, "Can stand and then move more than 50 metres but no more than 200 metres, either aided or unaided"

-- src:632 | | c. Can stand and then move unaided more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres. | 8 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor c (src:632)
`row for mobility 2c` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter c`, 8, "Can stand and then move unaided more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres."

-- src:633 | | d. Can stand and then move using an aid or appliance more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres. | 10 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor d (src:633)
`row for mobility 2d` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter d`, 10, "Can stand and then move using an aid or appliance more than 20 metres but no more than 50 metres."

-- src:634 | | e. Can stand and then move more than 1 metre but no more than 20 metres, either aided or unaided. | 12 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor e (src:634)
`row for mobility 2e` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter e`, 12, "Can stand and then move more than 1 metre but no more than 20 metres, either aided or unaided."

-- src:635 | | f. Cannot, either aided or unaided, –(i) stand; or(ii) move more than 1 metre. | 12 |
@ref Schedule 1, Part 3, activity 2, descriptor f (src:635)
`row for mobility 2f` MEANS `a row of Schedule 1` OF `mobility activity 2, moving around`, `letter f`, 12, "Cannot, either aided or unaided, –(i) stand; or(ii) move more than 1 metre."

GIVEN d IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 2`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`the row of a descriptor of mobility activity 2` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `mobility 2a` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2a`
    WHEN `mobility 2b` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2b`
    WHEN `mobility 2c` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2c`
    WHEN `mobility 2d` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2d`
    WHEN `mobility 2e` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2e`
    WHEN `mobility 2f` THEN JUST `row for mobility 2f`
    WHEN `no descriptor of mobility activity 2 applies` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 1, Part 3: all the rows, in the order of the table`

GIVETH A LIST OF `a row of Schedule 1`
`all the rows of the mobility activities table` MEANS
    LIST `row for mobility 1a`
       , `row for mobility 1b`
       , `row for mobility 1c`
       , `row for mobility 1d`
       , `row for mobility 1e`
       , `row for mobility 1f`
       , `row for mobility 2a`
       , `row for mobility 2b`
       , `row for mobility 2c`
       , `row for mobility 2d`
       , `row for mobility 2e`
       , `row for mobility 2f`
